
Instructions for building and publishing a new update site:

* Note that the Eclipse plugin works in tandem with a release of OpenJML.
The Uodate Site only holds the plugin per se, which defines the OpenJML
additions to the Eclipse IDE. The release of OpenJML contains the
OpenJML tool and the associated LSP server. When the Eclipse plugin
runs, it is connected to the LSP server (there is an OpenJML
Preference/Setting that tells teh plugi where to find the installation
of OpenJML and hence the location of the LSP server).

* Commit all changesa in OpenJMLUI, OpenJMLFeaeture, OpenJMLUpdateSite

* Be sure that the JMLAnnotations, OpenJMLsrc, OpenJMLUI, and Specs
  projects are built without errors and all unit and release tests pass

* Use the OpenJMLUI/release.sh script to set the new version number in the relevant
  .xml files and to build the new plugin jar files, copying them to the
  local clone of the openjml.github.io repository.

* Publish to https://openjml.org/eclipse-update-site by running
  git commit and git push in your local copy of the openjml.github.io repo.
